    description: "Found by the 2026-11-15 review of the stable-id items (reports and fixtures: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026). Re-run by hand the same day at dev e2b6ab8096, analyzer 9.2.0.\n\nDEFECT. Two functions each declare a local `struct Inner` with an init. A construction `Inner(x: 1)` inside the\nfirst function is bound to the second function's `Inner.init`.\n\nREPRO. ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/work/new/swift/src/a.swift:\n\n    func f() {\n        struct Inner { init(x: Int) {} ; func go() {} }\n        _ = Inner(x: 1)\n    }\n    func g() {\n        struct Inner { init(x: Int) {} ; func go() {} }\n        _ = Inner(x: 2)\n    }\n\n`hypergumbo run` gives two calls edges, f -> Inner.init at line 6 and g -> Inner.init at line 6. The init declared\nat line 2 has no caller.\n\nCAUSE, by reading. swift.py registers each symbol under its emitted name in one per-file dict\n(analysis.symbol_by_name[full_name] = symbol, e.g. :1175, :1646, :1656); both inits are named `Inner.init`, so the\nlater one replaces the earlier and every lookup returns it. The types themselves get distinct ids.\n\nRELATED, not the same. WI-muvab-dipik-luhik-tosug-valum-badoj-tagum-zufif: the two inits also tie on stable_id (a different consequence of the same naming).\nWI-joror-hizal-dutap-jajub-sodij-jijuj-lamil-dozuf: three other construction shapes (generic, Outer.Inner(...), inherited init).\n\nFIX DIRECTION. Resolve a construction against the types visible from the call site's enclosing scope (innermost\nfirst), not against a file-wide name.\n\nACCEPTANCE. On the fixture, f's construction binds the init at line 2 and g's the init at line 6; a top-level type\nwith a same-name function-local type elsewhere binds to the top-level one from outside that function.\n\nNOT CHECKED: classes and enums in the same position; methods (`Inner.go`) called on the constructed value; corpus\ncounts."  # f201
    fields: {}  # f201
