  message: "Fixed in PR #2200. Re-ran the filed fixture: on dev `f` bound the init of the same-named type local to ANOTHER function (line 6) and `h` bound a local init; now f binds its own type's init (line 2), g binds line 6, and a caller with no local type binds the top-level one (line 1). swift-composable-architecture: 150 of 11,930 call sites changed target, each to the type the caller's lexical scope sees; none lost; dead-code counts identical (816 / 352 / 464). A test pins that a missing member of a local type names nothing (my first mutation, `Outer.Missing.init` answered with Outer, survived until that test was added). NOT DONE (filed): a method or static call on a local type and a call to a local function still resolve by last-one-wins name; two same-named local types in two blocks of one function tie. NOT CHECKED: classes and enums in that position beyond the fixture, corpus counts. Repro record (both arms, commands and copied outputs): ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/pr2/tracker/repros.md; per-package detail: pr2/STATUS.md; churn: pr2/final_measure.txt."  # 73aa
